WEBVTT

00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:11.458
Itona had attacked Koro Sensei three times.

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:15.708
Lots of stuff happened,
but in the end, he finally joined our class.

00:00:15.708 --> 00:00:19.292
Then, a week later...

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:22.708
All right, class, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:28.125
I finally got paid, so I'm
heading out for some Shanghai crab!

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.042
<i>Yi</i>, <i>er</i>, <i>san</i>, go!

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:33.542
No fair leaving us out!

00:00:33.542 --> 00:00:37.042
Now that it's the second term,
our work's getting a lot harder.

00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:41.042
Koro Sensei's really trying
to get our grades up.

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:45.333
That's nice and all, but I haven't
picked up any girls in ages.

00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:51.958
You're sticking around, Itona?

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:54.417
"Tentacle"
You're sticking around, Itona?

00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:56.042
"Tentacle"
What are you making?

00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:57.792
"Tentacle"
Just what it looks like:

00:00:57.792 --> 00:00:59.708
an RC tank.

00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:01.500
Why?

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.042
I had an all-day cram session
with that octopus yesterday.

00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:07.917
It stressed me out.

00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:12.125
We'll save that for later.
Now for your next question.

00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:15.667
He really ticked me off...
so I'll use this to kill him.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:16.833
"Tentacle"

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:19.792
"Tentacle"
Just like Terasaka's dumb face told me...

00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:21.958
I can fail a hundred times.

00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:25.000
So I'll go kill him, expecting the worst.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.958
Go kill him? You mean...

00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:28.958
B-But this thing...

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:31.833
It's, like, crazy high-tech!

00:01:45.458 --> 00:01:48.125
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:50.958
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:56.417
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:59.083
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:01.792
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:05.583
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:09.583
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:12.542
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:02:12.542 --> 00:02:17.750
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:23.333
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:28.750
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:02:34.292 --> 00:02:36.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:39.583
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:42.375
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:44.958
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:47.667
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.375
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:53.208
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:53.208 --> 00:02:58.167
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
"Fourth Period: Spinning Time"
"by Masayoshi Kimura"

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.750
Is this for real?

00:03:10.042 --> 00:03:13.667
This thing uses cell phone camera parts.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:18.292
Wow, Itona...
You thought up these tweaks yourself?

00:03:18.292 --> 00:03:22.792
I learned basic electronics
at my old man's shop.

00:03:22.792 --> 00:03:26.750
Anybody could do it. Except Terasaka.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:31.042
Itona's changed so much
from when he had those tentacles.

00:03:31.042 --> 00:03:33.625
Tongue's as sharp as ever, though.

00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:45.292
Whoa!

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:09.500
Amazing... It's practically silent
when it moves <i>and </i>when it shoots!

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:14.417
I used a lot of electronic controls
to minimize gear noise.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:16.792
The camera feed is sent to the controller,

00:04:16.792 --> 00:04:19.292
moving in tandem with the main gun's sights.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.083
Wow, real spy stuff!

00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:24.250
Even if you <i>can </i>aim this at him...
where would you aim?

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:27.000
I'll let you guys in on something.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.375
There's one ideal place
we should be aiming for:

00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:31.542
our target's weak spot.

00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:33.708
Koro Sensei's weak spot?!

00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:37.792
He has a heart. Right under his tie.

00:04:37.792 --> 00:04:41.500
If we hit that, we can
take him down in a single strike.

00:04:46.042 --> 00:04:49.208
He'll probably have spread the word by now--

00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:50.667
about my weak point, that is.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:51.333
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #26: His heart"
about my weak point, that is.

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:56.167
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #26: His heart"
Assassination is bound to get a lot more fun with Itona in the mix.

00:04:58.625 --> 00:05:00.125
We can use this.

00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:01.250
Yeah.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:05.458
Okay, let's give it a test run
to prep for an assassination.

00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:08.875
If it breaks during the real deal,
we'll be clean outta luck.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:09.542
"Staff Room"

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.125
"Staff Room"
Dead slow ahead!

00:05:17.042 --> 00:05:19.250
Bye, Professor Bitch!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.875
See you later!

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:24.167
Go straight home, now--no detours.

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.208
We will!

00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:26.792
Want to stop for a snack?

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.167
Yeah, let's!

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.667
But you just said...

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:35.000
See anything?

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.958
No--the camera didn't get that far.
The field of view is too narrow!

00:05:39.958 --> 00:05:42.375
Can't we put in a bigger camera?

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.667
It'll increase the weight,
decrease its mobility,

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:48.292
and make target acquisition more difficult.

00:05:48.917 --> 00:05:50.375
In that case...

00:05:50.375 --> 00:05:53.583
Why don't we use a fisheye lens on the camera?

00:05:53.583 --> 00:05:55.042
"Advisor: Kotaro Takebayashi"
Takebayashi!

00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:55.250
"Correction" "Standard" "Fisheye"
Takebayashi!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.708
"Correction" "Standard" "Fisheye"
If we have the CPU correct any distortion in the received image...

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:03.125
"Correction" "Standard" "Fisheye"
even a small lens can get us a wide field of view.

00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:03.167
Got it.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.458
"Camera Crew: Taiga Okajima"
Got it.

00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:08.250
"Camera Crew: Taiga Okajima"
I'll find a small fisheye lens with a big viewing angle.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.500
Ritsu?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.625
Yes?

00:06:10.625 --> 00:06:13.042
Can you build a distortion correction program?

00:06:13.042 --> 00:06:17.167
Sure! I don't know what
you need it for, but I'll take care of it!

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:20.417
You're a genius, Takebayashi.

00:06:20.417 --> 00:06:22.375
We need a recording function.

00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:26.333
Yeah--it's a must for
effective analysis of our upgrades.

00:06:26.333 --> 00:06:29.125
And yet you were totally
turned off by an underwear thief.

00:06:29.125 --> 00:06:32.542
All in the name of assassination! Onward!

00:06:32.542 --> 00:06:35.250
Uh... Prototype 0!

00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:40.833
"High-Mobility Recovery Crew: Masayoshi Kimura"

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.792
"High-Mobility Recovery Crew: Masayoshi Kimura"
I'll go flip it over!

00:06:42.792 --> 00:06:44.667
Thanks, Kimura!

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.375
Shouldn't its suspension
be able to handle uneven surfaces?

00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:49.042
I'll come up with something.

00:06:49.042 --> 00:06:49.250
"Drive System Planning Support: Taisei Yoshida"
I'll come up with something.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.500
"Drive System Planning Support: Taisei Yoshida"
I know a little about drive systems and metalworking.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.917
This light khaki chassis color is too obvious.

00:06:55.917 --> 00:06:58.167
That's combat camouflage.

00:06:58.167 --> 00:07:02.375
It's got to blend into the school scenery,
or the target might notice it.

00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:03.833
I'm on it.

00:07:03.833 --> 00:07:04.333
"Camouflage Manager: Sosuke Sugaya"

00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:07.292
"Camouflage Manager: Sosuke Sugaya"
School camouflage. I'll paint it up.

00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:09.750
"Staff Room"
RC stuff is hardly human-sized.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.417
"Old Campus"
RC stuff is hardly human-sized.

00:07:10.417 --> 00:07:12.458
"Old Campus"
In the name of better maneuvering,

00:07:12.458 --> 00:07:13.125
"Road Map Cartographer: Hiroto Maehara"
In the name of better maneuvering,

00:07:13.125 --> 00:07:15.417
"Road Map Cartographer: Hiroto Maehara"
I'll draw up a map.

00:07:15.417 --> 00:07:15.708
I'll draw up a map.

00:07:15.708 --> 00:07:19.500
They really lose themselves
when smut's involved.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.917
So sleazy.

00:07:26.042 --> 00:07:29.000
"The Next Day"

00:07:29.583 --> 00:07:33.542
Hey. I finished the transmission yesterday.

00:07:33.542 --> 00:07:35.000
Hey, guys.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:35.125
I made us breakfast.

00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:37.083
"Provisions Supplier: Takuya Muramatsu"
I made us breakfast.

00:07:37.083 --> 00:07:41.708
How do you like this school camo?

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:47.000
You guys do realize that this is
all for an assassination plan, right?

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.750
Yeah, we know,
Mr. Student Council President!

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:53.708
All right, let's get in a test run
before the girls show up!

00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:54.875
Yeah!

00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:57.875
Nobody's tardy on a day like this.

00:07:57.875 --> 00:08:01.167
Ritsu starts up at eight o'clock sharp.

00:08:01.167 --> 00:08:02.833
I don't want to hurt her.

00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:04.708
Uh, yeah.

00:08:07.542 --> 00:08:08.458
Argh! You idiot!

00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:11.167
You gotta move carefully or it'll flip again!

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:12.958
Move! It's my turn!

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:17.000
There was no need to worry
whether the antisocial Itona

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.583
would fit in with our class.

00:08:19.583 --> 00:08:21.833
Smut and killing and making things:

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:27.667
Having hit all the boys' buttons,
they formed a circle around him.

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:30.792
Itona, we're all working on this together.

00:08:30.792 --> 00:08:34.458
Why don't you give this thing a code name?

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:36.458
I'll think about it.

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:42.958
The tentacles once asked me
what I wanted to be.

00:08:42.958 --> 00:08:45.333
When I said I wanted to be strong...

00:08:45.333 --> 00:08:48.125
soon that was all I could think about:

00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:52.000
hazy thoughts of fighting and winning.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.417
You can start with a fine thread.

00:08:54.417 --> 00:08:56.667
Over time, you'll spin it
into something stronger.

00:08:56.667 --> 00:09:01.583
Itona: "becoming thread."
My wish for you, right there in your name.

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:06.167
How did I ever forget my roots?

00:09:06.875 --> 00:09:09.833
Ack! It crashed! Terasaka, you suck at this!

00:09:09.833 --> 00:09:11.000
Say what?!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:16.125
--Hey, Itona, isn't this lever a little loose?
--This is probably where I should have started all along.

00:09:21.792 --> 00:09:23.833
A monster!

00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:25.958
--Run!
--No--fire!

00:09:28.042 --> 00:09:30.167
The main gun's nowhere near strong enough!

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.458
Gotta tweak that, too!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.625
Eeeyikes!

00:09:43.833 --> 00:09:47.292
Dammit...
To think we were done in by a weasel.

00:09:47.292 --> 00:09:51.000
Next time we'll need to
assign a driver and a gunner.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.542
You're on firing duty, Chiba.

00:09:52.542 --> 00:09:52.917
"Gunner: Ryunosuke Chiba"
You're on firing duty, Chiba.

00:09:52.917 --> 00:09:54.625
"Gunner: Ryunosuke Chiba"
Uh... okay.

00:09:55.583 --> 00:09:58.625
Mistakes are all part of
the development process.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.667
Itona I may have been a dud,

00:10:00.667 --> 00:10:02.667
"Itona I"
Itona I may have been a dud,

00:10:02.667 --> 00:10:03.458
"Itona I"
but we'll spin it into something stronger.

00:10:03.458 --> 00:10:06.250
but we'll spin it into something stronger.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.542
I can fail a hundred times,

00:10:08.542 --> 00:10:11.625
but I <i>will </i>kill him in the end.

00:10:11.625 --> 00:10:13.542
Hope I can count on you.

00:10:13.542 --> 00:10:15.250
You bet.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.917
Bloodlust is what binds us together.

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:20.292
This is going to be fun.

00:10:20.292 --> 00:10:25.667
All right! By March, we'll have this thing
looking up all the girls' skirts!

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:28.167
So that's our goal now?

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.250
What's this about up our skirts?

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.583
Kataoka!

00:10:31.583 --> 00:10:35.500
Nothing! We were talking about
side skirts on cars, that's all!

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.583
Oh, we heard you.

00:10:36.583 --> 00:10:37.958
Boys suck.

00:10:37.958 --> 00:10:40.542
And just who came up with the idea?

00:10:40.542 --> 00:10:42.583
I'm sure it wasn't <i>you</i>, Itona.

00:10:42.583 --> 00:10:45.250
--Okajima.
--Hey!

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.500
Good morning! Oh, Okajima!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:54.375
I have that fisheye lens
correction program ready for you.

00:10:54.375 --> 00:10:57.042
Wait! It wasn't just me! Right?

00:10:57.042 --> 00:10:59.875
Beats me. Don't pull me into this, Okajima.

00:10:59.875 --> 00:11:01.708
Maehara, you dirty rat!

00:11:01.708 --> 00:11:04.250
Just give it up, guys.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.875
Either way, it's clear you were
all in on this little scheme.

00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:10.250
Boys suck.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.833
What's going on?

00:11:11.833 --> 00:11:13.875
Kind of a crime of passion.

00:11:13.875 --> 00:11:15.000
Huh.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.500
No, it's, like, all adventurous!

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:22.042
You boys are impossible.

00:11:22.042 --> 00:11:26.042
Karma, I'm skipping today.
Show me a good spot.

00:11:26.042 --> 00:11:29.125
Wow, you can talk! Yeah, sure.

00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:32.083
Hey, you! Itona!

00:11:32.083 --> 00:11:35.417
Itona's tougher than we thought.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.000
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:11:40.542 --> 00:11:41.583
"Itona Horibe"

00:11:41.583 --> 00:11:45.750
"Itona Horibe"
Oh, so "Itona" is written with the characters for "becoming thread"?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.375
One of those flashy names!

00:11:47.375 --> 00:11:50.792
--Hey!
--It's a good name! Sounds cool.

00:11:50.792 --> 00:11:54.208
"Tentacle"
There are plenty of people with weird names in this class.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:12:00.875
"Masayoshi Kimura"
What? "Justice"?! I totally thought it was "Masayoshi!"

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.417
Everyone's generous enough
to read it that way, yeah.

00:12:06.417 --> 00:12:09.208
And I asked Koro Sensei to call me that, too.

00:12:09.208 --> 00:12:12.292
Sure made us nervous,
hearing your name at the entrance ceremony!

00:12:12.292 --> 00:12:13.750
Yeah, I guess.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:18.833
I hate the thought of another
public execution come graduation.

00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:21.375
Kimura's parents are police officers.

00:12:21.375 --> 00:12:21.917
"Justice"
Kimura's parents are police officers.

00:12:21.917 --> 00:12:23.292
"Justice"
They were so high on justice

00:12:23.292 --> 00:12:25.833
"Justice"
that that's what they named their child.

00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:31.625
And being my parents, they'd just
smack me if I complained about it.

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:36.250
They didn't think about how much
a kid could get teased in school.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.375
That's parents for you.

00:12:39.375 --> 00:12:43.042
Me, with this face--I'm Kirara. Kirara!

00:12:43.042 --> 00:12:45.250
Do I look like a Kirara to you?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:46.958
N-No...

00:12:46.958 --> 00:12:49.625
My mom lives in her own little fantasy world,

00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:51.417
but if something happens that she doesn't like,

00:12:51.417 --> 00:12:53.792
she goes into screaming hysterics.

00:12:53.792 --> 00:12:56.792
That's the kind of
stress-filled house I grew up in.

00:12:56.792 --> 00:13:01.167
No way was I going to
grow into my adorable little name.

00:13:01.167 --> 00:13:05.333
You've sure got it rough,
saddled with such weird names.

00:13:06.292 --> 00:13:06.542
"Karma Akabane"

00:13:06.542 --> 00:13:08.250
"Karma Akabane"
Oh, me?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:08.583
Oh, me?

00:13:08.583 --> 00:13:11.458
I actually rather like my name.

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:15.625
Guess some kids
inherit their folks' strange tastes.

00:13:15.625 --> 00:13:16.667
Hmm...

00:13:16.667 --> 00:13:20.125
I'm not satisfied
with how I was named, either.

00:13:20.125 --> 00:13:24.833
Huh? I though you liked "Koro Sensei."
Kayano named you that.

00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:27.625
I <i>do </i>like it. That's why I'm not satisfied.

00:13:27.625 --> 00:13:32.708
There are still two people
who won't call me by that name.

00:13:32.708 --> 00:13:37.833
Mr. Karasuma just says "Hey" or "You there."

00:13:37.833 --> 00:13:39.792
We're not some middle-aged married couple!

00:13:39.792 --> 00:13:45.708
But it's embarrassing for a
full-grown adult to be like, "Koro Sensei!"

00:13:46.375 --> 00:13:50.500
Then why don't we call each other
by code names instead?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.583
Code names?

00:13:51.583 --> 00:13:55.500
Yeah--we make new names for everyone.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.125
Like the assassins we met on the island:

00:13:58.125 --> 00:14:01.292
they called each other
by code names to hide their real ones.

00:14:01.292 --> 00:14:04.375
Don't you think it's kinda cool and assassin-y?

00:14:04.375 --> 00:14:07.000
I see. Good idea!

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:07.250
"Lottery Box"
I see. Good idea!

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:09.167
"Lottery Box"
Here's what we'll do:

00:14:09.167 --> 00:14:11.875
Write down your suggestions.

00:14:11.875 --> 00:14:15.833
We'll call each other
by the names I pull out of this box.

00:14:15.833 --> 00:14:19.000
Sounds fun, but do we have to
think up names for everyone?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:23.083
"Tentacle"
I'm just writing down whatever comes to mind.

00:14:23.083 --> 00:14:27.458
All right... using real names
is forbidden all day today!

00:14:27.458 --> 00:14:29.333
Whaaat?

00:14:32.708 --> 00:14:35.250
Baseball Geek, Baseball Geek!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.792
Any movement from the target?

00:14:36.792 --> 00:14:37.042
Nothing yet, Lanky Artist!

00:14:37.042 --> 00:14:39.167
"Code Name: Baseball Geek"
Nothing yet, Lanky Artist!

00:14:39.167 --> 00:14:42.583
"Code Name: Baseball Geek"
Da Densest is hiding in wait near a lone pine.

00:14:42.583 --> 00:14:44.000
Team President Poverty will come from behind,

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:44.250
"Code Name: President Poverty"
Team President Poverty will come from behind,

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.708
"Code Name: President Poverty"
chase him into the swamp,

00:14:46.708 --> 00:14:46.833
"Code Name: Hot-and-Cold Sniper"
chase him into the swamp,

00:14:46.833 --> 00:14:49.375
"Code Name: Hot-and-Cold Sniper"
and then Hot-and-Cold Sniper will fire on him.

00:14:52.333 --> 00:14:54.542
Okay--here goes!

00:14:54.542 --> 00:14:55.292
Shape up, you two!

